### Atlas Liquidity Platform — API examples (Layer 2)
#
# Install the "REST Client" VS Code extension (humao.rest-client), then click
# the "Send Request" link above each request.
#
# Requires Postgres:  docker compose up -d

@host = http://localhost:8081

### List all settlement accounts
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts
Accept: application/json

### Filter by currency — this is now a real SQL query with an index behind it
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?currency=USD
Accept: application/json

### Lowercase works too — normalised at the boundary
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?currency=usd
Accept: application/json

### Filter by jurisdiction (drives data residency from Layer 11)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?jurisdiction=EU
Accept: application/json

### Fetch a single account
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-EU-0001
Accept: application/json

### JPY has zero minor units — note the buffer has no decimal places
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-JP-0001
Accept: application/json

### --- Writes (new in Layer 2) ------------------------------------------

### Set a new liquidity buffer
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-US-0001/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "31000000.00"
}

### Send it again — PUT is idempotent, the result is identical
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-US-0001/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "31000000.00"
}

### Over-precise amount — Money rounds HALF_EVEN to the currency's minor units
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-SG-0001/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "9000000.0050"
}

### 400 — Bean Validation rejects this at the edge, with a field-level error
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-US-0001/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "not-a-number"
}

### 400 — missing field
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-US-0001/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

### 400 — malformed JSON is the caller's fault, so not a 500
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-US-0001/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{ this is not json

### 404 — unknown account, as an RFC 7807 problem detail
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-NOPE/liquidity-buffer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": "100.00"
}

### --- Errors and operations --------------------------------------------

### 404 on read
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-DOES-NOT-EXIST
Accept: application/json

### 400 — unknown jurisdiction, with an actionable message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?jurisdiction=ATLANTIS
Accept: application/json

### Supply your own correlation id and watch it appear in the service log
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts
X-Correlation-Id: dinesh-manual-test-001
Accept: application/json

### Health — now includes a real database check.
#   Try: docker compose stop postgres   and hit this again.
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Liveness probe (is the process alive?)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health/liveness

### Readiness probe (can it actually serve traffic?)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health/readiness

### Metrics — Hikari pool gauges appear here from Layer 2 onward
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/hikaricp.connections.active

### How long the pool made callers wait for a connection
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/hikaricp.connections.acquire
